§ `Part V - Termination of residential tenancy agreements`

§§ `Division 5 - General`

§§§ `76C. Fixed term tenancies continued as periodic tenancies`

DECLARE `fixed term expiry` HAS
    `the agreement creates a tenancy for a fixed term` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is terminated before the expiry day` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.76C
@export Decide whether a fixed-term residential tenancy agreement continues as a periodic tenancy after the expiry day under s.76C
GIVEN e IS A `fixed term expiry` @desc Applies to a fixed-term agreement unless it is terminated before the expiry day. It then continues as a periodic tenancy on the same terms that applied immediately before the expiry day, subject to any court modification under s.76C(3).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement continues as a periodic tenancy after the expiry day` IF
        e's `the agreement creates a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND NOT e's `the agreement is terminated before the expiry day`

§§§ `76. Compensation to lessor for holding over`

DECLARE `holding over` HAS
    `the tenant has failed to comply with an order for possession made by a court under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.76
@export Decide whether the lessor is entitled to compensation for holding over under s.76
GIVEN h IS A `holding over` @desc TRUE if the tenant failed to comply with a court order for possession made under Part V.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor is entitled to compensation for holding over` IF
    h's `the tenant has failed to comply with an order for possession made by a court under this Part`

§§§ `80. Recovery of possession of premises prohibited except by court order`

DECLARE `recovery of possession` HAS
    `a person has possession as a tenant under a residential tenancy agreement or as a former tenant holding over after termination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry is for the purpose of recovering possession of the premises or part of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry is under an order of a competent court` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.80
@export Decide whether a person is prohibited from entering to recover possession under s.80
GIVEN r IS A `recovery of possession` @desc No person shall, except under an order of a competent court, enter premises of which a person has possession as a tenant or former tenant holding over, for the purpose of recovering possession, whether entry is peaceable or otherwise.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must not enter to recover possession` IF
        r's `a person has possession as a tenant under a residential tenancy agreement or as a former tenant holding over after termination`
    AND r's `entry is for the purpose of recovering possession of the premises or part of the premises`
    AND NOT r's `entry is under an order of a competent court`

§§ `Fixtures`

`fixed term not terminated early` MEANS `fixed term expiry` WITH
    `the agreement creates a tenancy for a fixed term` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement is terminated before the expiry day` IS FALSE

`self help eviction` MEANS `recovery of possession` WITH
    `a person has possession as a tenant under a residential tenancy agreement or as a former tenant holding over after termination` IS TRUE,
    `entry is for the purpose of recovering possession of the premises or part of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `entry is under an order of a competent court` IS FALSE

#EVAL `the agreement continues as a periodic tenancy after the expiry day` `fixed term not terminated early`
#EVAL `the person must not enter to recover possession` `self help eviction`
#ASSERT `the agreement continues as a periodic tenancy after the expiry day` `fixed term not terminated early` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the person must not enter to recover possession` `self help eviction` EQUALS TRUE
